                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>On June 8, 1953, Lieutenant General William K.
                        Harrison and General Nam
                        Il signed the agreement which established the “Terms of Reference
                    for the Neutral Nations Repatriation Commission” culminating 18 months of
                    negotiations over Item 4 of the armistice agenda. For text of the agreement, see
                    Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, June 22, 1953, pages
                    866–868.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
